  Exponentiation
    The cartesian form takes integer exponents without difficulty. Yet it soon becomes tedious:

      z  =  a  +  j * b
      =>    z^3  =  (a  +  j * b) * (a  +  j * b) * (a  +  j * b)  =  (a^2  +  j * a * b  +  j * a * b  -  b^2) * (a  +  j * b)
                 =  (a^2  +  2 * j * a * b  -  b^2) * (a  +  j * b)
                 =  a^3  +  j * a^2 * b  +  2 * j * a^2 * b  -  2 * a * b^2  -  a * b^2  -  j * b^3
                 =  a^3  -  3 * a * b^2  +  j * (3 * a^2 * b  -  j * b^3)

    Ok. But what about z^1770 or z^1.618033989 ?
    We're dealing with exponentiation -- and we have access to an exponential form. Let's use it.

      |z|  =  √(a² + b²)    ;    arg (z)  =  atan2 (b, a)

      z  =  |z| * exp (j * arg (z))    =>    z^x  =  |a|^x * exp (j * arg (z) * x)  =  |z|^x * [ cos (arg (z) * x )  +  j * sin (arg (z) * x) ]
      |z^x|  =  |z|^x
      arg (z^x)  =  arg (z) * x
      Re (z^x)  =  |z|^x * cos (arg (z) * x)
      Im (z^x)  =  |z|^x * sin (arg (z) * x)

    Ok. But what if the exponent is also complex?
    Let's define:

      ζ  =  α  +  j * β
      =>    |ζ|  =  √(α² + β²)    &&    arg (ζ)  =  atan2 (β, α)    &&    ζ  =  |ζ| * exp (j * arg (ζ))  =  |ζ| * [ cos (arg (ζ)  +  j * sin (ζ) ]

      z^ζ  =  |z|^ζ * exp (j * arg (z))^ζ  =  |z|^ζ * exp ( j * arg (z) * (α  +  j * β) )  =  |z|^ζ * exp ( j * arg (z) * α  -  arg (z) * β) )
           =  |z|^ζ * exp (j * arg (z) * α) * exp (-arg (z) * β)

    We cannot solve |z|^ζ right away: it has an imaginary part in its exponent. The exponential function has been convenient so far. More please!
    Luckily enough:

      exp (ln (x))  =  x    and    ln (x^y)  =  y * ln (x)        //  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logarithm

    Then:

      |z|^ζ  =  exp ( ln (|z|^ζ) )  =  exp ( ζ * ln (|z|) )  =  exp ( α * ln (|z|)  +  j * β * ln (|z|) )  =  exp (α * ln (|z|)) * exp (j * β * ln (|z|))

    So:

      z^ζ  =  exp (α * ln (|z|)) * exp (j * β * ln (|z|)) * exp (j * arg (z) * α) * exp (-arg (z) * β)
           =  exp [ α * ln (|z|)  -  β * arg (z) ]  *  exp [ j * ( α * arg (z)  +  β * ln (|z|) ) ]

          |z^ζ|  =  exp [ Re (ζ) * ln (|z|)  -  Im (ζ) * arg (z) ]
      arg (z^ζ)  =  Re (ζ) * arg (z)  +  Im (ζ) * ln (|z|)

